  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946119/assets/5c7116b4ee933aacb284e0d9b16576b910166bf1e01f58a46931fc0636a933c5.png)\n\nFind the area (in square units) of $\u25b3ABC$ shown above.",
  "worked_solution": "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AB.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $m\u2220A={30}^{\u2218}.$ Notice that relative to $\u2220A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{\u2015}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{\u2015}{AB}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(m\u2220A) & =\\frac{BC}{AB} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}\u2061({30}^{\u2218}) & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}\\,x}{5x+2} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}\\,x}{5x+2} \\\\ \\sqrt{3}(5x+2) & =3\\cdot 2\\sqrt{3}\\,x \\\\ 5\\sqrt{3}\\,x+2\\sqrt{3} & =6\\sqrt{3}\\,x \\\\ 2\\sqrt{3} & =\\sqrt{3}\\,x \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =2\\sqrt{3}\\,x=2\\sqrt{3}\\cdot 2=4\\sqrt{3}, \\\\ AB & =5x+2=5(2)+2=12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $\u25b3ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot BC\\cdot AB \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\sqrt{3}\\cdot 12 \\\\  & =24\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
